      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Gardenstown, Lanesborough, Co. Roscommon, N39 TF21\nKeith McLoughlin of Sheehy Meares is delighted to bring to the market this impressive six-bedroom detached residence at Gardenstown, Lanesborough, Co. Roscommon, N39 TF21. Constructed circa 1980 and extending to approximately 237.45 sq. m., this substantial family home is set in a picturesque countryside location with panoramic views across Lough Ree and presents a truly rare opportunity in an exceptional setting.\nThe ground-floor accommodation comprises an entrance porch, a bright tiled hallway with a feature staircase, and an impressive open-plan sitting and dining room featuring four large windows, French doors and a striking back-to-back brick fireplace incorporating gas fires. A kitchen, breakfast room, three generously sized bedrooms and two WCs complete the ground floor.\nThe first floor continues the bright and spacious theme, with Velux windows allowing natural light to flow throughout. Accommodation includes a relaxing sitting room, three further bedrooms and a family bathroom featuring a large freestanding bath.\nThe standout feature of the accommodation is the first-floor sunroom, which enjoys breathtaking panoramic views across Lough Ree and the surrounding countryside.\nThe property stands on a mature site extending to approximately 0.593 acres, with established lawns, trees and shrubbery providing an attractive and private outdoor setting. A tarmacadam driveway, gated entrance and attractive stone boundary wall further enhance the exterior.\nThe property also benefits from a right of access to Lough Ree, offering a wonderful amenity for boating, fishing and enjoying the lakeside surroundings.\nGardenstown enjoys a peaceful rural setting while remaining only approximately 5 km from Lanesborough. Situated on the banks of the River Shannon at the northern end of Lough Ree, Lanesborough is a thriving waterside town renowned for its marina, boating, fishing and scenic walks. The town provides an excellent range of everyday amenities, including shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs, schools, sporting facilities and essential local services.\nThe adjoining village of Ballyleague offers additional amenities and contributes to the area?s lively community atmosphere.\nRoscommon Town is conveniently located approximately 10 km away and provides an extensive range of shopping, educational, recreational and professional services. The town is home to primary and secondary schools, supermarkets, independent retailers, cafés, restaurants, medical facilities and numerous sporting clubs. Roscommon Train Station also provides convenient rail connections to Dublin and the west of Ireland.\nThis is a superb family home combining an impressive 237.45 sq. m. of flexible accommodation, mature private grounds, magnificent lake views and an excellent location within easy reach of both Lanesborough and Roscommon Town.\nViewing is highly recommended.\n"
      },
